comment_regular_data.body:
@justinmk, @zeertzjq, @blami Thank you for the reviews! I rebased onto master, fixed news, added the leading-`%<` requirement, and I fixed all the out-of-date information that I could find for 'stl', 'ruf', and 'ru'.

I also added two workarounds to help with [HTML formatting](https://neovim.io/doc/user/options/#'statusline'). "- not applicable" was interpreted as a bullet point, and the fourth list item in the documentation for `%@` was consuming the documentation of the next 5 'stl' items (`<`, `=`, `#`, `$`, `*`).

The failing test looks unrelated ("API nvim_list_chans, nvim_get_chan_info stream=job :terminal channel").
